        {
          "path": "_m/d/j/w/q/cockspur-island-light-wp/cockspur-lighthouse-at-fort-pu.jpg",
          "filename": "Cockspur Lighthouse at Fort Pulaski- Notice the high water line at the base of the lighthouse. Current projections indicate sea (74fecef1-c085-befd-7c2c-5d8abd81c732).jpg",
          "caption": "Cockspur Lighthouse at Fort Pulaski: Notice the high water line at the base of the lighthouse. Current projections indicate sea level in this area may rise as much as 2.3 feet over the next 50 years.\nKeywords: cocksupur lighthouse; climatechange",
          "alt": "Cockspur Lighthouse at Fort Pulaski: Notice the high water line at the base of the lighthouse. Current projections indicate sea level in this area may rise as much as 2.3 feet over the next 50 years.\nKeywords: cocksupur lighthouse; climatechange",
          "width": 1280,
          "height": 961,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "NPS photo",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cockspur_Lighthouse_at_Fort_Pulaski-_Notice_the_high_water_line_at_the_base_of_the_lighthouse._Current_projections_indicate_sea_(74fecef1-c085-befd-7c2c-5d8abd81c732).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "cockspur-island-light-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "djwq",
          "smallPath": "_m/d/j/w/q/cockspur-island-light-wp/cockspur-lighthouse-at-fort-pu-small.webp"
        },
        {
          "path": "_m/d/j/w/q/cockspur-island-light-wp/growing-cockspur-island-lighth.jpg",
          "filename": "Growing - Cockspur Island Lighthouse (b0e60b1e-ba0a-4293-8578-bd415e839280).jpg",
          "caption": "Black and white image of a small three-story white brick lighthouse with a dock.\nCockspur Island Lighthouse, late 1800s.  Erected in 1856, the lighthouse has stood as a symbol of guidance, survival, and preservation. A specially built dock allowed lightkeepers to access the lighthouse even during high tide. Today, climate change \nthreatens the lighthouse, so it is closed to the public.\nKeywords: Cockspur Island Lighthouse; Centennial; Fort Pulaski National Monument; Fort Pulaski; cockspur island; lighthouse",
